# NOTICE — native Qwen3-TTS 0.6B CustomVoice executor

## 1. Specifications implemented from upstream references

No upstream source file was copied into `native/tts/`, `native/tts_cli/` or
`native/tts_tests/`. The math, tensor names, shapes and constants were derived
by reading the following Apache-2.0 sources on the build host and
cross-checking numeric outputs against them. The C++/CUDA implementation is
original work in this repository.

- `qwen_tts` Python package, Apache-2.0
  - `qwen_tts/core/models/modeling_qwen3_tts.py` — talker and code-predictor
    transformer, GQA, half-rotation mRoPE, RMSNorm, SiLU-gated MLP, greedy
    generation, repetition penalty, prompt/frame embedding assembly.
  - `qwen_tts/core/tokenizer_12hz/modeling_qwen3_tts_tokenizer_v2.py` —
    speech codec decoder: split residual vector quantizer, causal Conv1d
    padding, ConvTranspose1d right-trim, ConvNeXt block, SnakeBeta activation,
    dilated residual units, waveform decoder block order.
- HuggingFace Transformers, Apache-2.0
  - Qwen2 byte-level BPE tokenizer conventions, GPT-2 `bytes_to_unicode`
    mapping, safetensors tensor loading, `RepetitionPenaltyLogitsProcessor`
    semantics, causal mask and RoPE helpers.
- safetensors file format specification, Apache-2.0 — header and
  `data_offsets` byte layout only.

Only formulas, identifiers and dimensional conventions were taken. No code
text was reproduced.

## 2. Code reused from the in-repository ASR slice

Three files are byte-for-byte copies of the repository's own native ASR
implementation under `native/umm_asr_native/`, which is original Apache-2.0
work produced for the earlier ASR vertical slice and carries the
`SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` header in every file:

- `native/tts/bf16.hpp`        (identical to `native/umm_asr_native/bf16.hpp`)
- `native/tts/safetensors.hpp` (identical to `native/umm_asr_native/safetensors.hpp`)
- `native/tts/safetensors.cpp` (identical to `native/umm_asr_native/safetensors.cpp`)

These are generic, model-independent primitives (BF16 round-to-nearest-even
storage and the safetensors container reader). They contain no ASR-specific
logic. All TTS-specific CUDA kernels in `native/tts/cuda_kernels.cu` were
written for this slice; `cuda_kernels.hpp` differs from the ASR counterpart.

## 3. Runtime dependencies (linked, not embedded)

- NVIDIA CUDA 12.4 runtime (`libcudart.so.12`) — system-provided on the build
  host under the NVIDIA EULA. Only the runtime library is linked; no CUDA
  sample or SDK source is embedded.
- ICU (`libicuuc`, `libicui18n`, `libicudata`) — ICU License (permissive,
  Unicode/IBM). Used for NFC normalization and the Unicode regex in the BPE
  tokenizer. Linked dynamically; no ICU source is included.
- nlohmann/json — MIT License. Header-only, consumed for `config.json`
  parsing.
- C++ standard library, libc, pthreads, dl/rt — platform system libraries.

No Python, PyTorch, SGLang or the `qwen_tts` package is linked or invoked at
run time. `ldd umm-tts-native` lists only the libraries above.

## 4. Determinism statement

The talker applies repetition penalty once per distinct group-0 id. Duplicate
history entries are marked through an idempotent shared-memory bitset, then
one thread per logit applies the penalty; the earlier duplicate read/modify/
write race was removed in Task #59. Real-CUDA duplicate fixtures and the
recorded direct/stage A/A replays are byte identical on the tested SM90 path,
including generated frames and PCM16. This is not a claim for unseen prompts,
the unrun full two-GPU R4 replay, other hardware, or perceptual quality; see
`TTS_NATIVE.md` and `docs/realtime-first-audio.md`.
